Package: epistle
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: podman (>= 5.0), podup
Suggests: postgresql
Description: self-hosted mail server with a management API and CLI
 epistle is a headless mail server: SMTP, IMAP4rev2, JMAP and POP3 with the
 modern email-security stack (SPF, DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS, TLS-RPT, ARC, DANE,
 SRS) and ACME certificates for the mail protocols. It has no web UI of its
 own — administration goes through the `epistle` command or the management
 HTTP API, which is closed to the network by default.
 .
 A production deployment runs as a rootless Podman stack alongside
 PostgreSQL, which is why podman and podup are recommended. The binary also
 runs standalone for the management commands, for `epistle config-check`,
 and for key generation, import and export, none of which need a container
 runtime.
